  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce complete C and C++ packages before source-free offline installation. Independent C11/GMP and C++20 callers replay unchanged after physical relocation, giving four replay executions plus two setup executions per selection. The standalone result-only API projects checked-record payloads through Array and Option results without checked-input metadata. Independent controls reject every missing record and coordinated report, resource, model and package mutation. Nested checked-record C/C++ acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete packages from two roots. Independent C11/GMP and C++20 callers install offline after author removal and replay after physical relocation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. Constructor/source entry counts and peak memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted or glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance.",
